Thanksgiving was upon us. My mom had commandeered the space, barking orders at my dad while he hovered at the edges, trying to be helpful without stepping on her toes. Liam was there too, charming as ever, peeling potatoes as if he belonged here. His sleeves were rolled up, his forearms dusted with flour from a pie crust he’d volunteered to help with, earning my mom’s approval in record time.

