I sat on the couch, pulling Liam’s hoodie tighter around me, my fingers absentmindedly fiddling with the pearl necklace around my neck. The soft hum of the dishwasher filled the silence.

Liam stretched his legs out in front of him, his arm draped casually along the back of the couch. “Well,” he said, grinning, “your cousins are fun.”

I smiled, the warmth from earlier lingering. “They’re like my siblings. They’ve been grilling every guy I’ve ever brought around since I started dating Thanks for being a good sport”

“Ben was ready to kill me.” Liam’s grin widened.

