“Liam is fine,” I said, but that was a mistake. The cushions felt deeper than they were a minute ago, or maybe I’d just stopped trying to hold myself up.

Because Ben’s eyes lit up. “Fine?” he repeated, sitting up. “Just fine? Damn, that’s a downgrade from Thanksgiving.”

