Ava shifted closer on the bed, folding her legs underneath her. “Hey,” she said gently. “What happened?”

I didn’t answer right away. My pulse felt muffled, like it was echoing from somewhere deeper than it should’ve been.

“I know I’m younger,” she added, brushing a strand of hair off my face. “But we’ve always trusted each other. Right?”

There was no pity in her tone. Just quiet concern.

I turned toward her, eyes bleary, but steady. “You’ve never been one hundred percent honest with me either.”

