Liam’s breath was hot against my throat, his lips trailing lower, slower, each press deliberate, knowing. His hands skimmed beneath my sweater, fingers brushing over bare skin, his touch searing, possessive, worshipping.

“You don’t know what you do to me,” he murmured, his voice low, rough with restraint. I did, because he did the same to me.

My fingers threaded into his hair, pulling him closer, needing more, needing him, needing this.

He exhaled sharply as I tilted my hips beneath him, the delicious press of his body against mine sending heat curling low in my stomach.

“Caroline,” he groaned, his grip tightening, his control hanging by a thread.

