Because Liam claimed me in that moment, kissing me like he had been starving for me, like he could never get enough. His hands explored every inch of skin he could reach, every curve, every dip, his touch reverent but unrelenting. He shifted, his weight pressing into me in a way that made my breath stutter, my head spin, the heat between us building, rising, devouring.

