Until I knew, without a doubt, that I was exactly where I belonged. Wrapped in him. Completely his.

Liam’s hands roamed over my body with a slow, deliberate hunger, like he had all the time in the world to reacquaint himself with every inch of me. His touch was possessive, knowing, as if he were tracing over old paths, committing them to memory again.

