I arched into him, my body already reacting before my mind could catch up. His fingers skimmed under the hem of my sweater, pushing it higher, teasing against my ribs.

“I missed you,” I admitted, and Liam stilled for half a second before letting out a low groan, his grip tightening on my waist.

“Tell me you love me,” he demanded, his voice deeper, rougher.

“I love you,” I breathed, and it was like something inside him snapped.

