He shifted, pressing me further into the mattress, his weight, his heat, the sheer presence of him surrounding me. My thighs parted instinctively as he settled between them, the hard press of him against me sending a shiver down my spine.

“Liam,” I gasped, clutching at his sweater, needing more, needing him.

His hand slid up my thigh, pushing fabric aside, fingers teasing against bare skin.

“Tell me what you need,” he murmured, his lips brushing over my jaw, teasing, taunting. I swallowed hard, every nerve in my body sparking, alight.
“You,” I whispered. “I need you. I need you inside of me.”

A sharp exhale, his forehead dropping to mine, his grip tightening like he was barely holding on.

“Say it again,” he demanded. “Liam—”
“Again.”

“I need you inside me,” I said, stronger this time, unafraid.

His lips crashed into mine, this time with no restraint, no hesitation, just raw, unfiltered need.

He pulled my sweater over my head, his hands skimming bare skin, worshiping, reverent, but never slow.

“Fuck,” he muttered, his lips trailing lower, kissing, tasting, marking. Stripping me as I clawed off his own clothes.

The air between us crackled, heavy with heat, with everything unspoken, with every inch of space that had existed between us for too long.

And now, there was no space. No room for anything but him.
Liam’s fingers slipped lower, teasing, his smirk evident even as he dragged his lips along my throat.

“I hope you know,” he murmured, his breath hot, his voice wrecked. “I’m not stopping until I hear my name again. And again. And again.”

And when he finally gave me what I wanted—what we both wanted— I said it.
Again.

And again.

And again.

Until there was nothing left of me but Liam.


The knock on the door sent a jolt of panic through me, my breath catching as I scrambled upright, yanking the sheets around me like armor.

