Liam shot me a pointed look. “Do I look like someone who regrets that decision?” “He still can’t play to this day,” Michael said, shaking his head. “It’s a tragedy.” “It’s a miracle,” Liam corrected.
“Caroline, you play, don’t you?” Diane asked suddenly.

